Installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js project.

IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS:
======================

1. Package Installation:
   - Installed @vercel/speed-insights@2.0.0 using pnpm
   - Package added to dependencies in package.json

2. Code Changes:
   - Modified: src/app/layout.tsx
     * Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
     * Added <SpeedInsights /> component at the end of the body tag
     * Component placed after ThemeProvider and AuthProvider to ensure proper initialization

3. Implementation Notes:
   - Followed official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router (v13.5+)
   - Used the framework-specific import from '@vercel/speed-insights/next'
   - SpeedInsights component is placed in the root layout to ensure it runs on all pages
   - Component is positioned at the end of the body to avoid blocking page rendering
   - Preserved existing code structure, providers, and styling

4. Files Modified:
   - package.json - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
   - pnpm-lock.yaml - Updated with new dependency tree
   - src/app/layout.tsx - Added SpeedInsights component

5. Verification:
   ✓ Build completed successfully (no errors)
   ✓ Linter passed (only 1 pre-existing warning unrelated to changes)
   ✓ TypeScript compilation successful
   ✓ All 10 routes generated without issues

NEXT STEPS:
===========
To complete the Speed Insights setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel project dashboard
3. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics after deployment

The implementation follows Next.js App Router best practices and is ready for production deployment.
